{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["Its plates — a mold shaped like an open box for making the bread in." "And its bowls — for the need of the two bowls of frankincense, as it is written: ונתת על המערכת לבונה זכה." "And its supports and its holders — explained in Menachot. Because the bread was two arrangements, six per arrangement, one on top of the other, and they would fork out on both sides toward the table. And the supports, which were like half-tubes from fork to fork — the bread rested on the supports, and likewise between bread and bread that were six, one on top of the other; and therefore elsewhere they are called קשות הנסך — because they provide shelter over the bread, between bread and bread." "With which it is covered — by the supports, as I explained."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {2 "Reading מסככין as 'provide shelter/covering,' from the root סכך; קשות הנסך (Exodus 37:16) is read by Rashbam as 'the covering supports,' from סכך."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:43:05.913821373Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}